# Lambda Labs Cloud

Local credentials already exist on this machine. Prefer them over asking the user for keys.

## Credentials (do not commit or paste secrets)

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `~/.config/lambda/api_key` | Cloud API key |
| `~/.ssh/lambda.pem` | SSH private key for account key **Lambda SSH** |
| `~/.config/lambda/README.md` | Longer local notes |

```bash
export LAMBDA_API_KEY="$(cat ~/.config/lambda/api_key)"
```

Auth: `Authorization: Bearer $LAMBDA_API_KEY`  
Base: `https://cloud.lambdalabs.com/api/v1`  
Docs: https://cloud.lambdalabs.com/api/v1/docs

Use **curl** for API calls. Plain `urllib` without a browser-like User-Agent can get HTTP 403.

## Common API calls

```bash
# List running instances
curl -sH "Authorization: Bearer $LAMBDA_API_KEY" \
  https://cloud.lambdalabs.com/api/v1/instances

# Capacity + types (check regions_with_capacity_available)
curl -sH "Authorization: Bearer $LAMBDA_API_KEY" \
  https://cloud.lambdalabs.com/api/v1/instance-types

# Launch (always include ssh_key_names: ["Lambda SSH"])
curl -sH "Authorization: Bearer $LAMBDA_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"region_name":"us-east-1","instance_type_name":"gpu_1x_a10","ssh_key_names":["Lambda SSH"],"quantity":1}' \
  https://cloud.lambdalabs.com/api/v1/instance-operations/launch

# Terminate
curl -sH "Authorization: Bearer $LAMBDA_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"instance_ids":["INSTANCE_ID"]}' \
  https://cloud.lambdalabs.com/api/v1/instance-operations/terminate
```

Account SSH keys: **Lambda SSH** (use with `lambda.pem`), also `miRNA-Interaction-Transformer`.

## SSH

```bash
ssh -i ~/.ssh/lambda.pem ubuntu@<INSTANCE-IP>
# Optional alias (HostName may be stale — update from /instances IP first):
ssh lambda
```

Default user is `ubuntu`. After launch, wait until the instance is active and has an IP before SSHing.

## Agent habits

- Check `/instances` before launching; avoid duplicate machines.
- Prefer types with non-empty `regions_with_capacity_available`.
- Terminate when finished; GPU time is billed while running.
- Never commit `api_key`, `*.pem`, or instance secrets into the repo.
